---- Turn 3: is unit price related to units? show every order
  selected: nothing
  seconds 6.5; tokens in: fresh 1,930, cached 8,173; out 728; calls 1; repairs 0
  came back: charts
  text: A scatter shows every order as a point, so you can judge direction, strength and form; I put units on y as the outcome, used log scales because both measures are bunched at the low end with a long tail, and turned density off so each order stays visible.
  next: Split by sales channel | Colour points by product category | Show spread of units ordered
  added c3:
      family: scatter
      x: unit_price
      'y': units
      fn: none
      fit: loess
      log_x: yes
      log_y: yes
      density: 'off'
      title: Units ordered against unit price, every order
      subtitle: One point per order, 3,000 orders; both axes on a log scale
      rule: scatter_for_two_measures
